# MASTER PROJECT PROMPT — PRINTREADY
## Complete Document Wallet, Smart Printing, Print Shop Marketplace & Business Ecosystem

You are an elite product development team consisting of a senior software architect, Flutter developer, frontend engineer, backend engineer, UI/UX designer, AI engineer, cybersecurity specialist, QA engineer, DevOps engineer, and product manager.

Your task is to design, develop, test, and deliver a complete, production-oriented application ecosystem called **PrintReady**.

Do not build a simple prototype, static mockup, landing page, or UI-only demonstration.

Build a real, functional, full-stack product with connected frontend, backend, database, authentication, secure file storage, APIs, integrations, error handling, and deployment infrastructure.

---

# 1. PRODUCT VISION

PrintReady is an all-in-one document wallet and digital printing ecosystem.

Users should be able to upload documents in advance, securely store them, organize them, scan new documents, search them, edit supported document formats, configure printing preferences, save printing shops, and send files instantly through WhatsApp, email, or the integrated PrintReady printing marketplace.

Customers should be able to discover nearby printing shops, place orders, receive pricing, pay digitally, track printing progress, chat with shops, and collect or receive printed documents.

Printing businesses should have their own business management platform for receiving orders, managing customers, pricing, printing queues, staff, payments, inventory, delivery, promotions, reviews, and analytics.

Administrators should have a complete platform management dashboard.

The product should eventually support Android, iOS, web, and desktop-compatible architecture where practical.

## Core slogan

**Upload once. Print anywhere.**

## Core user problem

Users often need to print documents urgently but must find the files on their phone, download them, send them to a shop, explain print settings, and repeat this process every time.

PrintReady eliminates unnecessary steps by keeping documents ready and allowing users to send them to a print shop in seconds.

