# 2. DEVELOPMENT RULES

Follow these rules throughout development.

1. Build a real working application.
2. Do not create fake buttons or nonfunctional screens.
3. Do not simulate successful uploads, payments, orders, authentication, or integrations.
4. Do not use hardcoded fake data in production functionality.
5. Use realistic mock data only in clearly labeled development/demo mode.
6. Every interactive element must have a working action.
7. Every feature must have its own functional implementation or a clearly documented integration requirement.
8. Maintain a feature checklist.
9. Do not silently omit features.
10. Do not replace requested features with simplified alternatives without documenting the limitation.
11. Build in development milestones, but maintain the complete product scope from the beginning.
12. Maintain architectural consistency across customer app, shop app, web portal, and admin dashboard.
13. Prioritize Android as the primary mobile platform initially.
14. Design the architecture to support future iOS and web deployment.
15. Follow secure development practices.
16. Never expose API secrets, private keys, payment credentials, or server secrets in frontend code.
17. Never claim an integration is functional if credentials or approvals are missing.
18. If an external integration requires credentials, create its integration layer, configuration, setup documentation, and testing framework.
19. Handle errors gracefully.
20. Preserve existing working features when adding new functionality.
21. Do not rewrite stable components unnecessarily.
22. Use modular, maintainable, reusable code.
23. Write documentation alongside development.
24. Use automated testing wherever possible.
25. Before marking a feature complete, test its complete workflow.

